NNAAMMEE
     ddeellaayy..44tthh — FreeBSD debugging boot module

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The file that goes by the name of ddeellaayy..44tthh is a set of commands designed
     to add debugging capabilities to loader(8).  The commands of ddeellaayy..44tthh by
     themselves are not enough for most uses.  Please refer to the examples
     below for the most common situations, and to loader(8) for additional
     commands.

     Before using any of the commands provided in ddeellaayy..44tthh, it must be in‐
     cluded through the command:

           include delay.4th

     This line is present in _/_b_o_o_t_/_b_e_a_s_t_i_e_._4_t_h file, so it is not needed (and
     should not be re-issued) in a normal setup.

     The commands provided by it are:

           ddeellaayy__eexxeeccuuttee          Executes the [string] procedure stored in
                                  the ddeellaayy__ccoommmmaanndd environment variable after
                                  llooaaddeerr__ddeellaayy seconds.

                                  If the optional ddeellaayy__sshhoowwddoottss environment
                                  variable is set, a continuous series of dots
                                  is printed.

                                  During the duration, the user can either
                                  press Ctrl-C (or Esc) to abort or ENTER to
                                  proceed immediately.

     The environment variables that effect its behavior are:

           _d_e_l_a_y___c_o_m_m_a_n_d
                     The command to be executed by ddeellaayy__eexxeeccuuttee.

           _l_o_a_d_e_r___d_e_l_a_y
                     The duration (in seconds) to delay before executing
                     ddeellaayy__ccoommmmaanndd.

           _d_e_l_a_y___s_h_o_w_d_o_t_s
                     If set, will cause ddeellaayy__eexxeeccuuttee to print a continuous
                     series of dots during the delay duration.

FFIILLEESS
     /boot/loader      The loader(8).
     /boot/delay.4th   ddeellaayy..44tthh itself.
     /boot/loader.rc   loader(8) bootstrapping script.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Introducing a 5-second delay before including another file from
     _/_b_o_o_t_/_l_o_a_d_e_r_._r_c:

           include /boot/delay.4th
           set delay_command="include /boot/other.4th"
           set delay_showdots
           set loader_delay=5
           delay_execute

